<<<
pigeon)(dove. Used absolutely, the words are coextensive in application, every d. being a p., & vice versa; but p. is the ordinary word, & d. is now the rarity, suited for poetical contexts, symbolism, &c.
===
**pigeon)(dove.** Used absolutely, the words are coextensive in application, every *d.* being a *p.*, & vice versa; but *p.* is the ordinary word, & *d.* is now the rarity, suited for poetical contexts, symbolism, &c.
>>>

<<<
D. is also still used without special significance of particular kinds of pigeon, especially the turtle & other natives, but not of exotics; & much more often the kind is specified, as in stock, ring, turtle, -d.
===
*D.* is also still used without special significance of particular kinds of pigeon, especially the turtle & other natives, but not of exotics; & much more often the kind is specified, as in *stock, ring, turtle, -d.*
>>>

